; Restores 31 weapon variants whose inventory icon renders as a cropped
; fragment of an unrelated gun, or as an empty cell, in the inventory and in
; the F7 debug spawner.
;
; Same fault as mod_system_..._fix_rpk74_hd_icon.ltx, found by auditing every
; section in the merged system.ltx for the signature that produced it:
;
;   ini_sys:dltx_get_filename_of_line(sec, "icons_texture")
;        ~= ini_sys:dltx_get_filename_of_line(sec, "inv_grid_x")
;
; MartinLore's Stalker 2 icons repoints a weapon family at one of its HD
; atlases by patching only the family's parent section, e.g.
;
;   ![wpn_fal_aus]  icons_texture=ui\ui_stalker2_rifles  12x4 @ (0,12)  scale=2
;
; Scoped and kitted variants inherit icons_texture and inv_grid_scale from
; that patched parent, but they redeclare inv_grid_x/y/width/height of their
; own, and those are still the legacy ui_icon_bas / ui_icon_equipment
; coordinates from the weapon's own config. MartinLore patches the variants
; it knows about; the ones below it never names, so nothing corrects them.
;
; The engine then samples a legacy-sized window at legacy coordinates out of
; a 4096x2048 HD atlas, and draws it in a ceil(w/scale) x ceil(h/scale) cell.
; wpn_fal_aus_kit_aus_tri, for instance, reads 300x100 px at (450,600) -- the
; muzzle half of the SA-58's own HD icon -- into a 3x1 cell instead of the
; parent's 600x200 px at (0,600) in 6x2. Every section listed here was
; checked by cropping the rect out of the atlas it actually resolves to:
; all 31 are a crop of a neighbouring gun, a splice of two, or blank space.
;
; Fix, as with the RPK-74: delete the four stale coordinates so the
; inheritance the override was silently breaking is restored. DLTX drops a
; "!key" line in the base+mods merge (IsMergingBaseAndMod, Xr_ini.cpp), so
; the parent's value survives the parent merge that follows.
;
; Deleting rather than reassigning, again for the same reason. None of these
; sections declares icons_texture or inv_grid_scale of its own; both reach
; them only by inheritance from MartinLore's patched parent. Writing HD
; coordinates here would be wrong without the icon pack installed, and would
; leak inv_grid_scale to anything inheriting further down the chain
; (wpn_ak101_camo_1p29 et al. inherit wpn_ak101_camo, not wpn_ak101).
;
; With the icon pack installed each variant draws its parent's HD icon: the
; right gun, at the right size, minus the scope that distinguished it. Every
; parent listed was verified to render correctly. Without the pack they fall
; back to the parent's legacy icon instead of their own -- a near-identical
; gun, and nothing garbled. A DLTX patch cannot be conditioned on another
; mod's presence, so that is the tradeoff.
;
; Filename sorts after every mod_system_*_s2*.ltx in the icon pack
; (s2pistols carries the longest z-run, 18) so these deletions apply last.

